// Title: Deletion of Volume Shadow Copies via WMI with PowerShell
// ID: 21ff4ca9-f13a-41ad-b828-0077b2af2e40
// Status: test
// Level: high
// Author: Tim Rauch, Elastic (idea)
// Date: 2022-09-20
// Tags: attack.impact, attack.t1490
// Description: Detects deletion of Windows Volume Shadow Copies with PowerShell code and Get-WMIObject. This technique is used by numerous ransomware families such as Sodinokibi/REvil
// Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

process where (((process.command_line like "*_.Delete()*" or process.command_line like "*_Remove-WmiObject*" or process.command_line like "*_rwmi*" or process.command_line like "*_Remove-CimInstance*" or process.command_line like "*_rcim*")) and ((process.command_line like "*_Get-WmiObject*" or process.command_line like "*_gwmi*" or process.command_line like "*_Get-CimInstance*" or process.command_line like "*_gcim*")) and (process.command_line like "*_Win32_ShadowCopy*"))
